            <ArticleTitle>Update on percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>321-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty was first performed in a human coronary artery in 1977. In this article, we review the possible mechanisms of angioplasty, current indications for angioplasty, and complications of angioplasty including acute closure and restenosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
